# VTID-03943 — commands run during this change

## Investigation (via background Explore agent, then independently verified)
Agent audited discover-feed/search, notifications, community-members,
reminders, shop-feed, click-redirect, intent/cover-generation,
journey-checklist, campaigns across both repos looking for a genuine
cross-repo (backend+frontend) gap. Reported the discover-search
`hidden_breakdown` undercounting bug as its top finding, with the caveat
that the frontend (HiddenByLimitationsFooter.tsx, useMarketplace.ts) was
already fully wired to render `past_purchases` — no frontend code change
was strictly required.

Independently verified by reading the actual files:
$ grep -n "past_purchases\|hiddenBreakdown" services/gateway/src/routes/discover-search.ts
  327-329 (hiddenBreakdown literal — no past_purchases field)
  347-349 (withoutPast computed, never counted)
  460-461 (hidden_total = sum(hiddenBreakdown) — past-purchase drops invisible)
$ grep -n "past_purchases" services/gateway/src/routes/discover-feed.ts
  218,219,243 (the correct inline pattern this fix mirrors)

Confirmed zero existing test coverage for either route:
$ grep -rl "past_purchases" services/gateway/test
(no results, before this VTID)
$ cat services/gateway/src/routes/discover-search-repository.ts | head -5
  "impact-allow-no-test: pure data-access seam... zero coverage today" —
  this repo's own documented exception for why discover-search.ts has no
  route-level test; informed the decision to fix via an extracted, pure,
  independently-testable helper instead.

## Fix
services/gateway/src/services/limitations-filter.ts:
  Added excludePastPurchases<T extends {id:string}>(allowed, pastPurchases)
  -> {withoutPast, past_purchases_hidden} — pure, no I/O.

services/gateway/src/routes/discover-search.ts:
  1. Import excludePastPurchases.
  2. Seeded hiddenBreakdown's initial literal with past_purchases: 0 (so its
     inferred type carries the field through every reassignment).
  3. The ctx-present branch (line ~338) now also carries past_purchases
     forward explicitly when reassigning hiddenBreakdown from
     result.hidden_breakdown (which has no past_purchases field of its own).
  4. Replaced the inline past-purchase filter with a call to
     excludePastPurchases(), folding past_purchases_hidden into
     hiddenBreakdown — this is the actual bug fix.

services/gateway/src/routes/discover-feed.ts:
  Replaced its own already-correct inline computation with a call to the
  same new shared helper, so the two routes cannot independently drift
  again the way this bug shows they can.

## New test file (written from scratch)
services/gateway/test/limitations-filter.test.ts — 6 tests, pure function,
no mocking required: basic filter, correct count with multiple matches,
zero-overlap case, empty-past-purchases case, empty-allowed-list case, and
a past-purchase entry with no matching product contributing nothing.

